# =====================================================================
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT (unchanged by the Vercel deployment adapter)
# =====================================================================
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"
SESSION_SECRET="change-this-to-a-long-random-string"
PORT=4001
NODE_ENV=development

# STORAGE_DIR unset (below, commented out) -> local filesystem storage under
# apps/server/storage/files, exactly as before. Set BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN (Vercel section below)
# to switch to Vercel Blob even locally, if you want to test against it; leave it unset for the
# plain local-disk workflow.

# =====================================================================
# VERCEL PRODUCTION (Vercel deployment adapter — see
# docs/architecture/…-vercel-deployment-adapter.md for the full rationale)
# =====================================================================
# Set these in the Vercel dashboard's Environment Variables UI, never in a committed file.
#
# NODE_ENV=production                     — set automatically by Vercel for deployed environments.
#
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL="libsql://your-db-name.turso.io"
#   The Turso/libSQL database URL (see src/lib/prisma.ts). Required together with
#   TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN — the app refuses to start in production with only one of the two set. When
#   both are present, PrismaClient connects through the libSQL driver adapter instead of a local
#   file; when TURSO_DATABASE_URL is unset (the local-development case above), nothing about
#   PrismaClient's construction changes from before this adapter existed.
#
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN="<a Turso database auth token — a secret, never commit>"
#   Authenticates the connection above.
#
# TRUST_PROXY=1
#   Vercel's own edge network is the one reverse-proxy hop in front of this app in production —
#   see src/lib/trustProxy.ts. (Locally/in development this app uses no reverse proxy at all;
#   leave TRUST_PROXY unset there, matching the section above.)
#
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN="<provisioned automatically when Vercel Blob storage is attached>"
#   Selects the Vercel Blob storage backend in src/lib/storage.ts — when this is unset, the app
#   uses local-filesystem storage (STORAGE_DIR, unchanged). Vercel sets this itself once Blob
#   storage is attached to the project; it does not need to be typed in by hand.
#
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL="https://smartcomputinglab.org"
#   Enables GET /sitemap.xml (served at the document root — see src/routes/sitemap.routes.ts and
#   vercel.json's rewrites). Must be the app's real public origin (protocol + host, no trailing
#   slash). GET /robots.txt works either way; it only omits its "Sitemap:" line when this is unset.
#
# MAX_IMAGE_BYTES=5242880           (optional; same defaults/meaning as local development below)
# MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES=15728640

# =====================================================================
# Shared settings, either environment (unchanged from before this adapter)
# =====================================================================

# Phase 26 — client-IP trust policy (see src/lib/trustProxy.ts for the full rationale). REQUIRED
# in production; development/test default to 0 (no reverse proxy) if left unset.
#   TRUST_PROXY=0  no reverse proxy in front of this server; X-Forwarded-For is never trusted.
#   TRUST_PROXY=1  exactly one trusted reverse-proxy hop that strips any client-supplied
#                  X-Forwarded-For before setting its own — the one topology this app's tests
#                  and docs certify (see docs/architecture/phase26-…), and the value to use on
#                  Vercel (see the VERCEL PRODUCTION section above).
# TRUST_PROXY=0

# Phase 26 — enables GET /sitemap.xml (served at the document root, not under /api — see
# src/routes/sitemap.routes.ts). Must be the public origin the SPA is actually served from
# (protocol + host, no trailing slash). GET /robots.txt works either way; it only omits its
# "Sitemap:" line when this is unset. Left unset by default rather than a fabricated domain.
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL="https://labs.example.edu"

# Phase 13 — file/media storage. STORAGE_DIR is where uploaded blobs live (metadata only in
# SQLite); it must stay outside apps/web/dist and is never served by express.static. Defaults to
# apps/server/storage/files if unset. Ignored when BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN is set (Vercel Blob
# backend — see the VERCEL PRODUCTION section above and src/lib/storage.ts). MAX_IMAGE_BYTES /
# MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES override the default per-category size limits (5 MB / 15 MB) documented in
# packages/shared/src/schemas/files.ts, on either storage backend.
# STORAGE_DIR="./storage/files"
# MAX_IMAGE_BYTES=5242880
# MAX_DOCUMENT_BYTES=15728640
